 "text": "We spend most of our time indoors, so the air inside matters. Cooking, cleaning and even breathing all affect it. The simplest step is to open a window for a few minutes each day. Fresh air replaces the stale air inside. When you cook, turn on the fan above the stove. Clean dust regularly with a damp cloth, which traps the dust instead of spreading it. Some people add plants, although their effect is small. If your home is near a busy road, open windows on the quieter side. Clean air helps you sleep and think better. These small steps cost almost nothing, and they make a home more pleasant every day."
